===Etymology===
From {{der|en|NL.|anabaptista}}, from the {{der|en|grc|ἀναβαπτισμός}}, itself from {{m|grc|ἀνα-|t=re-}} and {{m|grc|βαπτισμός|t=baptism}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A member of a [[radical]] [[wing]] of [[Christian]]s during the [[Protestant]] [[Reformation]], with a tenet of adult baptism.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author=[[w:Toni Morrison|Toni Morrison]]|title=[[w:A Mercy|A Mercy]]|publisher=Chatto & Windus|page=95|passage=Were the '''Anabaptists''' right? Was happiness Satan’s allure, his tantalizing deceit?}}
# A member of any of several [[present-day]] [[church]]es descended from that origin.
#: {{hypo|en|Mennonite|Amish|Hutterite|Brethren|Dunker|Dunkard|River Brethren}}

